read_theory — resource-read tool mirror (DECIDED, planned)
==========================================================

status: planned (2026-07-15)
2026-07-12 "flagged, not scheduled" note.
spec: "resource-read tool mirrors" under "mcp resources".
umbrella: plans/resource_tool_mirrors (assumptions, shared uri-handler
factoring, autonomous_proving bundle, resource suppression).

what it is: a builtin tool alias for the isabelle://theory/{name}
resource. rationale (updated 2026-07-30): the primary human-in-the-loop
mode reaches resources by user @-mention; claude code DOES let the
model read resources autonomously (RESOLVED POSITIVE 2026-07-15 — this
plan carried the stale "UNVERIFIED" until 2026-07-30), which relieves
urgency without removing the requirement, since clients that surface
resources to humans only still need tools and a fully-autonomous mode
still wants the reads as tools it is nudged to call. the twin tools are
that model-invoked surface. ships registered-but-inactive; the
autonomous_proving bundle activates it. the invariant these serve —
every declared resource, users' included, is reachable as a tool — is
in the umbrella.

advertised metadata (sketch)
----------------------------

name          read_theory
description   "Read a theory's source text. Accepts any theory the
              session structure knows — image, loaded, or filesystem
              tier (AFP included when registered). `lines` selects a
              window, e.g. \"120-180\"; without it an oversized
              theory returns the first window plus a truncation
              note. Same content as the isabelle://theory/{name}
              resource."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "name": {"type": "string"},
                 "lines": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["name"]}
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}

backing: zero new mechanism. the handler is a thin call into the
same resolution path resources/read uses for isabelle://theory/{name}
(image_theory normalization -> tier resolution -> Ir.source /
snapshot node source / session-structure path map; ?lines= slicing
and truncation rules included). if implemented, factor the uri
handler so tool and resource share one function — the tool must
never grow behavior the resource lacks, and (added 2026-07-30) never
LACK behavior the resource has; either direction is drift.

tests (sketch): [scala unit] row + dispatch + parity with the
resource read on Fake_Backend; [e2e] read a filesystem-tier theory
by tool and by resource, assert byte-identical payloads.
